                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Just finished getting 100% achievements in the game. This was a really nice experience.\n\nIt's fairly slow paced, but chock full of personality and detail. Most of the puzzles are fairly logic based and not too hard to solve, but the 'secrets' you need to discover for the third ending can be pretty cryptic to find.\n\nThe vibes and art style of the game are fantastic, very reminiscent of old 90's pc games, complete with uncanny visual and grimy pseudo realistic textures. Certain segments of the game gave me flashbacks to playing old 'edutainment' games on my grandma's old bulky mac pc.\n\nI would not call the game very 'scary', or disturbing, but I play a ton of horror games so that could just be me being numb. Take that with a grain of salt. I've seen other reviews that call the game fairly disturbing. Even if you don't find the game 'scary', the world and experience are still fantastic and I loved it enough to play through multiple times to get all the endings.",
